From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LosDaemons13 <esteveloris@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvn: a host segment hangs off the recording's bytes in the
 block it overflowed from
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pokémon Violet 4.0.0 (a derived profile) aborted on an iPhone 17 Pro just
after the opening, at frame 9,668: FATAL NVN command list 0x710c311400:
record {op 60557, size 16} at 0x16a7807a8, 1960 bytes into its piece of
1968 at 0x16a780000, in nvn_queue_submit. The piece starts a 256 KB host
segment, and the bytes there are another recording's (a compact record,
then op 14 of 24 bytes). By then the host had lent 19,456 segments, about
two a frame.

Cause: a segment hung off [the recording's first record, the write
position at the overflow). Violet's command buffers each take fixed-size
blocks of one allocator from their memory callback (main+0x2652b50 in
4.0.0, which ignores the size asked for and adds the next block of its
list, or a null pool when the allocator is empty), and several render
workers record at once. A recording that ran through several blocks had
its first record in an earlier block, so the range covered the blocks of
other command buffers in between; when one of them was given out, the
segment was freed, the next overflow took it and recorded over it, and the
first recording was submitted afterwards.

Fix: cmd_new_segment moves a recording's begin to the start of each
segment it continues in, so a segment hangs off the recording's bytes in
the block it overflowed from, never wider. With nothing of the recording
there, it hangs off the byte at the write position, and off the block's
last byte when that position is the block's end (the byte past it is
another block's).

t_nvn 5b''': a command buffer records through two 1 KB blocks with
another command buffer's block between them, a 1,400-byte update goes to
a host segment, the block between is given out (the segment stays lent), a
third command buffer overflows (it gets another segment), and the first
recording replays whole; giving out the block it overflowed from frees
the segment.

Checked: hle_nvn.c and t_nvn.c compile for arm64-apple-ios26.0 with
-Wall (LLVM-MinGW clang and the iOS 27.2 SDK, on Windows), test_docs.
Not run: t_nvn itself and regress.py (they need an Apple-silicon Mac),
Violet on the device after the fix.

New reference entry: docs/reference/nvn-objects.md, "A host segment
reclaimed through another command buffer's block"; Violet's note updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Pokémon Violet aborted on the iPhone just after the opening (a host segment freed and recorded over before its recording was submitted)
Issue: none yet (LosDaemons13/NX2Apple, Pokémon Violet 4.0.0 crash after the opening on an iPhone 17 Pro)

